From: ARLinux maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] nls: Backport valid Kurdish and Papiamento sort locales

Backport Wine bccb0f31c806472c061c65ae33d808aa58761ecd and
c17e773a1c67d7b82f7fb021cc729b92b15f6a20 by Piotr Caban.
Regenerate locale.nls with tools/make_unicode after applying this patch.
.NET Framework enumerates these names through CultureInfo.TextInfo; dangling
sort-locale references cause CultureData.STEXTINFO to throw NullReferenceException.
Use Debian's byte-identical archive for the ISO table: SIL currently returns 403.
The upstream SHA-256 check remains unchanged.

--- a/tools/make_unicode
+++ b/tools/make_unicode
@@ -49,1 +49,1 @@
- iso639    => { url  => "https://iso639-3.sil.org/sites/iso639-3/files/downloads/iso-639-3_Code_Tables_$ISO639VERSION.zip",
+ iso639    => { url  => "https://sources.debian.org/data/main/w/wine/10.0~repack-12/debian/unicode/iso-639-3_Code_Tables_$ISO639VERSION.zip",
@@ -1071,1 +1071,1 @@
- { name => "ku-Arab", lcid => 0x00007c92, group => 13 },
+ { name => "ku-Arab", lcid => 0x00007c92, group => 13, sortlocale => "ku-Arab-IQ" },
@@ -1246,1 +1246,1 @@
-## name => "pap-029", lcid => 0x00000479 },
+ { name => "pap-029", parent => "pap", file => "pap", lcid => 0x00000479 },
